 ### Fixed
+- **`ctx_edit` no longer fails when `old_string` was copied from a compressed
+  `ctx_read` view.** Modes like `aggressive` strip blank lines and comments and
+  halve indentation, so the quoted text did not exist verbatim on disk. When the
+  exact, CRLF and trailing-whitespace matches all miss, `ctx_edit` now matches
+  the non-blank lines of `old_string` (whitespace-trimmed), allowing only
+  blank/comment lines in between. The match must be unique. The edit is applied
+  as a line diff onto the original span, so stripped blank lines and comments
+  are kept, and inserted lines get their indentation mapped back to the file's.
